 ### Differentiable Mesh Refinement
-A training strategy that refines the tetrahedral mesh by subdividing vertices with high color gradients. It differs by focusing on gradient-based adaptive refinement for neural rendering rather than fixed hierarchical subdivision steps [984-differentiable-mesh-refinement.md].
+A training strategy that refines the tetrahedral mesh by subdividing vertices with high color gradients to increase resolution where needed, aiming to solve the issue of wasted resolution in empty regions [S1, unofficial]. It differs by focusing on gradient-based adaptive refinement for neural rendering rather than fixed hierarchical subdivision steps [984-differentiable-mesh-refinement.md].
 
 ### Recursive Subdivision
-A general approach to mesh refinement. It differs by potentially using arbitrary subdivision rules, whereas 3-root-2 uses a specific 3-step geometric insertion sequence [1304-recursive-subdivision.md].
+A general approach to mesh refinement that applies subdivision rules iteratively [G]. It differs by potentially using arbitrary subdivision rules, whereas 3-root-2 uses a specific 3-step geometric insertion sequence [1304-recursive-subdivision.md].
 
